  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8aba985e-9c91-485b-a9c4-65591f8e39aa",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "__Step 4:__\n",
    "\n",
    "Extracting the links for all books from all pages."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "d293f42f-9375-408b-8564-06443bf03cee",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Initializing a list to store the result (all links)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "c2317a1f-0bca-4086-8683-512e808b4f0d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Iterate over all pages from the website and always collect all links\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4d140985-358e-44bf-9ad5-17edc4250d83",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<div class=\"alert alert-block alert-info\">\n",
    "    <b>Exercise 1c </b>: Iterate over the extracted links and extract the product information as a list of dictionaries. The information we are interested in are:\n",
    "    <ul>\n",
    "        <li> title </li>\n",
    "        <li> category </li>\n",
    "        <li> price </li>\n",
    "        <li> star-rating </li>\n",
    "     </ul> \n",
    "    The result should look like this [{'name': 'name_of_book1', 'category': 'category_of_book1', 'price': 'price_of_book1', 'rating': 'star_rating_of_book1'}, {'name': 'name_of_book2', 'category': 'category_of_book2', 'price': 'price_of_book2', 'rating': 'star_rating_of_book2'}, ...]). \n",
    "    Transform the dictionary into a pandas dataframe. \n",
    "</div>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5bcea333-f635-4297-a196-925f6f5173d1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "__Step 1:__\n",
    "\n",
    "When being asked to scrape information from several sub-pages or items, it is always heplful to start with one URL-link, build the scraper for this URL (so that it works properly) and then modify it into a loop over the different URLs.\n",
    "Therefore, we will start with the first items URL and cinstruct the crawler."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "05c6a44e-06ed-4c7d-89b6-160a8aa7e00a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "18aa40a4-7065-4696-84bb-a1abc78b8b82",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Aaaand again. Head over to the website and investigate where to get the desired information like name, category and price"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "6f2ef728-f944-42be-9257-d5b9b56028ea",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Access subpage"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "6c2ef0f0-66df-455a-a6e7-3d7f19826ff2",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Get the title\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "40e34f85-1136-4ff2-8326-2436488e6575",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Get the category\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "69dc3986-609a-4289-89c0-d6e670f4639c",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Get the price\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "bc23fab9-4b78-4da7-aa9f-ada2cabc25dd",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Find the star ratings\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b762b2da-fab3-4113-b2ad-a7c16a8ce801",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The problem with `soup.find_all` the the case of the starratings is that below each detailed product page, we have book-reccomendations, each with their own ranking. So if we search `find_all`, we get all but are only interested in the first rating.\n",
    "\n",
    "`select_one` can help here. It returns the first element that matches the search attributes:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "603a2157-dfc4-4e35-824a-1313d8e4429a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "soup.select_one('p.star-rating') # the first match\n",
    "\n",
    "print(soup.select_one('p.star-rating').attrs) #it's attributes as a dictionary\n",
    "\n",
    "print(soup.select_one('p.star-rating').attrs.get('class')) # the actual rating"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "77e1d4fe-3ebf-4d10-b569-53f2e5bd38bb",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "rating = soup.select_one('p.star-rating').attrs.get('class')\n",
    "rating[1]\n",
    "\n",
    "# we are interested in the second list-element --> rating[1]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "fd9dae67-b091-4961-b570-f94d879d88de",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Now that we found the desired information for one single link, we have to construct the loop around these find-statements, in order to return the information for all links in the item_urls list"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "2280a84b-e925-424c-b32d-58ddba14898f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "877b2d6c-0bfa-4b86-92d3-0da22cc3788f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Initializing lists for all the information"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c581498d-d369-42a3-a31b-972c5e29a675",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "To combine the information into the desired dictionary-format, we need to use the zip function. Zip 'merges' single lists, by always pairing up the first, second, third, ... element of the provided lists.\n",
    "\n",
    "This way, we can combine title, price, category and rating of each book into a list."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "c6f2545c-eae2-417c-b0ab-3c7068ad58ae",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": []
  },
  {
