   "source": [
    "**Summary: Webscraping - Cookbook**\n",
    "\n",
    "- Inspect the websites HTML code, that you want to crawl --> where do you find the desired information\n",
    "- Access URL of the website (using an agent) and store the HTML content\n",
    "- Format/parse the content into a readable format\n",
    "- Extract/Filter the desired information and save it into a structured format (like a data frame or dictionary)\n",
    "- For information displayed on multiple sub-pages of the website, you may need to repeat steps 2–4 to have the complete information\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0f85fac8-e033-4300-a4fc-3baa0817b304",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Best practices:**\n",
    "\n",
    "- Only scrape if you are allowed to\n",
    "\n",
    "- Reduce the load on websited by setting a crawler delay (a waiting time before the next request-iteration)\n",
    "\n",
    "- Scrape resposibly and efficents (only what you need and keep privacy concerns in mind)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "74b88fde",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "***\n",
